n that's true that's a huge problem  you get a prescription for after some  medical procedure or an accident from a  doctor you become addicted you start  buying the same pills on the street you  realize heroin is cheaper so you switch  to the heroin the prescription opiates  for so many people  devastatingly have been a gateway to  street heroin that's a real problem  cannabis has not been shown to be a  gateway drug and there's actually a ton  of science about it you can go to Google  Scholar and you can read lots of studies  about it and the general findings after  I reviewed several dozen studies about  this are that there actually is a  correlation between very heavy cannabis  use and the use of harder drugs but the  problem is that that's deceptive and  that's as far as many people go there  are many people who will say well look  studies have shown that really heavy  cannabis users are more likely to also  be users or abusers of heavier drugs  there must be some causal relationship  this is a very different issue  altogether and we shouldn't conflate  what's going on a heavy cannabis user  could be more likely to get into harder  drugs regardless of their cannabis use  and regardless of the legality of  cannabis what I mean by that is if you  are the type of person who either for  biological reasons or circumstantial  family environmental reasons are more  likely to end up using heroin or cocaine  and crystal meth or whatever you are  also more likely to do that regardless  of whether cannabis is legal I hope I'm  being clear and what I'm saying here now  there is one way in which marijuana or  cannabis can be a gateway drug and it's  actually something that suggests we  should be legalizing it being around  drug-related violence being around drug  related guns and criminality and drug  dealing and that is happening in an  illicit way is going to put you in  situations where there are likely going  to be users of  heavier drugs around you you could get  sucked into it or into violence or  criminality simply by being around the  scene but that's actually an argument  for the legalization of cannabis to get  people who choose to use it away from  situations and circumstances where there  are heavier drugs or there are guns or  there is violence that is the way in  which cannabis being illegal can serve  as a gateway not just to using hard  drugs but also to getting people into  situations of criminality and violence  that are generated by cannabis being  illegal so back to Joe Biden it's no  surprise that this is what he's saying  he's being upfront and I disagree with  his position so the one thing I'm not a  Biden guy but this is yet more evidence  that Biden's not progressive the one  thing I appreciate that Joe Biden is  doing this election cycle and I've said  this before and some people get mad for  me pointing this out but it's true Joe  Biden doesn't seem to be pretending to  be a progressive in other words he makes  very clear on the stage he's not into  this medicare-for-all thing that other  people are talking about he makes it  very clear when he's asked I think  cannabis is a gateway drug and I  wouldn't legalize it  I disagree vehemently or as I like to  say vehemently even though I don't even  know where I heard it I just find it  funny I disagree vehemently with Joe  Biden on these positions but he's not  playing coy the way some other  candidates have been doing and it makes  it really clear that Biden's not the guy  for me I don't have to dig too deep to  figure that out so he's not the person I  want as the progressive as the  Democratic nominee rather he's not the  person I want as president but he's  being upfront with us he's completely  wrong but he is being upfront with us  here
 

